  "full_response": "# **Slack Webhook Integration Guide**\nThis guide will help you set up and use **Incoming Webhooks** in Slack to send automated messages to channels or users.\n\n---\n\n## **1. Set Up a Slack Incoming Webhook**\n### **Step 1: Create a Slack App**\n1. Go to **[Slack API: Your Apps](https://api.slack.com/apps)**.\n2. Click **\"Create New App\"**.\n3. Choose **\"From scratch\"**, name your app (e.g., `Webhook Bot`), and select your workspace.\n4. Click **\"Create App\"**.\n\n### **Step 2: Enable Incoming Webhooks**\n1. In your app dashboard, go to **\"Incoming Webhooks\"**.\n2. Toggle **\"Activate Incoming Webhooks\"** to **ON**.\n3. Click **\"Add New Webhook to Workspace\"**.\n4. Select the channel where messages should be posted (e.g., `#general` or a DM with yourself).\n5. Click **\"Allow\"**.\n\n### **Step 3: Copy Your Webhook URL**\nYou’ll see a **Webhook URL** like this:\n```\nhttps://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n```\n⚠️ **Keep this URL secure!** Anyone with it can post messages to your Slack channel.\n\n---\n\n## **2. Send a Message via Webhook**\n### **Basic cURL Example**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H 'Content-type: application/json' \\\n--data '{\n  \"text\": \"Hello, Slack! :wave:\",\n  \"channel\": \"#general\"\n}' \\\nhttps://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n```\n\n### **Example Payloads**\n#### **1. Simple Message**\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"This is a test message from a webhook!\",\n  \"channel\": \"#alerts\"\n}\n```\n\n#### **2. Message with User Mention**\nTo mention a user (`@username`), use their **Slack User ID** (e.g., `U12345678`).\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"<@U12345678> Please review this update!\",\n  \"channel\": \"#dev-team\"\n}\n```\n",
